I have a box in my hand.
I hold that box in front of the camera.
My father looks at the box.
He asks, "Maya, what is in your box?"
I happily open that box.
I say, "Papa, there are Indian sweets in this."
I show them the sweets.
"Look, this is my favorite pedha."
"And this is kaju katli."
"Who makes these sweets?" Papa asks.
"There is a shop near my house," I say.
"That uncle makes these nice sweets."
There are very colorful sweets in the box.
Papa smiles and says, "It looks very nice."
I pick up one pedha.
I say, "These sweets are for you too."
"But you are very far away!"
Papa says, "You eat one pedha for us."
I smile and eat that sweet pedha.
